<Legal title={'Accessibility statement'} eyebrow='Accessibility' meta='Last reviewed: October 11, 2026' lede='Albena is meant for everyone in the household. We work toward the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. We are not there yet, and this page says plainly where we are.' description='Albena works toward WCAG 2.2 AA but does not yet fully conform. Scope, what we checked, known gaps and how to report a barrier.'>
<section id="status"><h2>Where we are today</h2><p>albena.ai and the Albena customer portal <strong>do not yet fully conform</strong> to WCAG 2.2 level AA, and we do not claim conformance. On October 11, 2026 we completed an internal assessment using automated checks and a review of the source code, and fixed the problems on albena.ai and in the portal sign-in pages that it found. The scope table below shows what each product covers.</p><p>We have <strong>not</strong> had an independent audit. We have <strong>not</strong> yet tested with screen readers (VoiceOver, NVDA, JAWS), Voice Control, Switch Control or Dragon, so automated results do not tell us how these tools behave with our pages. Automated tools find only part of the problems that exist.</p></section>
<section id="scope"><h2>Scope</h2>
<div class="tbl-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Accessibility scope by product">
<table>
<caption class="sr">Accessibility status by product</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Product</th><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Website</th><td>albena.ai</td><td>Working toward WCAG 2.2 AA. Internal assessment done, known issues fixed; known gaps below. Not independently audited.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Customer portal</th><td>account.albena.ai</td><td>Same standard. Sign-in, invitation and account pages were checked from a built copy. Account pages that are drawn after sign-in (dialogs, tables, error states) were reviewed in code only.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Albena HUD</th><td>The Albena screen in your home</td><td>Assessed, not fixed yet. Several known gaps (see below).</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Obvera web console</th><td>Obvera (our IT service platform)</td><td>Assessed, not fixed yet. Several known gaps (see below).</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">iOS and macOS apps</th><td>Native apps</td><td>Out of scope. They do not yet have VoiceOver labels, and we do not claim VoiceOver, Larger Text or Reduce Motion support for them.</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div></section>
<section id="measures"><h2>What already works</h2><ul><li>One main heading per page, a logical heading order and landmark regions (header, navigation, main, footer).</li><li>A &ldquo;Skip to content&rdquo; link and keyboard operation with a visible focus indicator on albena.ai and the portal.</li><li>Automated contrast checks pass in light and dark appearance on every albena.ai page and every portal page we built and tested.</li><li>Labelled form fields, text error messages and status messages announced to screen readers. Form fields for your own name and email allow your browser to fill them in.</li><li>Pages reflow without sideways scrolling at a 320 pixel width. We checked this with an automated script on every albena.ai page and on the portal sign-in, check-your-email, invitation, privacy and accessibility pages.</li><li>Animation is switched off when your system requests reduced motion.</li><li>Voice conversations in the HUD have live captions and a transcript, three caption sizes and a reduce-motion switch.</li><li>Portal sign-in offers passkeys (no verification check) and a one-time code that you can paste.</li></ul></section>
<section id="limits"><h2>Known gaps</h2><ul><li><strong>Verification check on forms.</strong> The waitlist and support forms, and the portal email sign-in, use Cloudflare Turnstile to block spam. We configure it to run without a challenge when it can, but we have not verified that it never shows one, and an interactive challenge could be hard for some people. Each form has an email address next to it that you can use instead. Portal passkey sign-in does not use a verification check.</li><li><strong>Appearance.</strong> albena.ai and the portal are dark only. There is no light theme and no special high-contrast or forced-colors styling yet.</li><li><strong>HUD.</strong> Some status chips do not read their live values to screen readers. Single-key shortcuts cannot yet be switched off. The HUD status bar scrolls sideways on very narrow screens. Some small text there has too little contrast. The PIN entry uses spinning digit wheels with no paste or password-manager route.</li><li><strong>Voice is not the only way, but typing is not complete yet.</strong> Albena can be controlled by voice. A typed or switch-based way to give any command is not yet available in the HUD. If speech is hard for you, tell us and we will prioritise it.</li><li><strong>Obvera.</strong> Some table rows and icon-only buttons cannot be reached or named by keyboard and screen reader users, and some light-theme text has too little contrast.</li><li><strong>Apps.</strong> The iOS and macOS apps are not yet accessible with VoiceOver.</li><li><strong>Home page illustration.</strong> The product illustration is a visual mock-up with a text description. It is not interactive.</li></ul></section>
<section id="feedback"><h2>Tell us about a barrier</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:omar@dbaomarhuertasllc.com?subject=Accessibility%20barrier">omar@dbaomarhuertasllc.com</a>, or use the Accessibility topic on the <a href="/support#contact">support form</a>. Tell us the page, what you were trying to do and the assistive technology you use. We aim to reply within 2 business days and to fix confirmed barriers within 30 days, or tell you when.</p><p>If you are not satisfied with the reply, ask us to escalate in a reply or write &ldquo;Escalate&rdquo; in the subject line. We will respond in writing within 10 business days. You can also ask for content in another format.</p></section>
<section id="technical"><h2>Technical details</h2><ul><li><strong>Standard:</strong> WCAG 2.2 level AA.</li><li><strong>Status:</strong> partially conformant. We have not completed a conformance evaluation.</li><li><strong>Assessment approach:</strong> self-assessment on October 11, 2026 with axe-core in headless Chrome (light and dark appearance), an automated 320 pixel width reflow check and a manual review of the source code. No independent audit. No testing yet with screen readers, Voice Control, Switch Control or Dragon.</li><li><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> October 11, 2026. We will update this date whenever the statement changes.</li></ul></section>
<p class="legal-note">Related: <a href="/security">Security &amp; trust</a>, <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/support">Support</a>.</p>
</Legal>

